irectly from the visuals. The baseline report mentions its charts but does not integrate them as deeply into the narrative; the text describes the charts at a high level without extracting detailed insights from them. The candidate's visuals are more integral to the argument.\n\nOverall, the candidate report is clearly better than the baseline in all three sub-dimensions. The baseline has minimal, somewhat broken visuals with weak integration, while the candidate uses multiple professional, appropriate, and well-explained charts that actively support the insights. The candidate's visual presentation is more polished, insightful, and effectively communicates the analysis.",
