        "analysis": "Visual Clarity & Professionalism: The candidate report is significantly better. It uses clear, well-labeled charts (scatter plots, bar charts, line charts) with descriptive titles and captions embedded in the narrative, creating a professional and integrated feel. The baseline report has only a single, generically described visualization ('Cash Flow Impact Visualization'), lacking detail and integration. Candidate earns a positive score for superior layout and visual presentation.\n\nChart Appropriateness & Accuracy: The candidate report excels by using multiple chart types appropriate for the analytical tasks: scatter plots for filtering and risk/volatility relationships, bar charts for categorical breakdowns (account types), and line charts for trends (cash flow and risk over time). This matches the narrative's focus on trends, comparisons, and distributions. The baseline report's single, unspecified chart type for cash flow impact is less informative and lacks the same level of accurate, multi-faceted visual encoding. Candidate is better.\n\nText–Visual Synergy & Insightfulness: The candidate report demonstrates strong synergy, explicitly referencing each chart (e.g., 'The following scatter plot visually confirms...', 'The bar chart below breaks down...') and using visuals to highlight key trends, clusters, and improvements described in the text. The narrative connects visual patterns to insights. The baseline report's text mentions a chart only once in a generic way, with minimal explanation of what it shows or how it supports the findings. The candidate's visuals are integral to the insight delivery, while the baseline's feel decorative and disconnected.\n\nOverall, the candidate report is clearly superior across all three sub-dimensions.",
