        "analysis": "Sub-dimension 1 (Visual clarity & professionalism): The baseline report contains only one simple bar chart comparing top 10 conversation tags for two customer segments. While clean and functional, it's minimal in design. The candidate report demonstrates significantly stronger visual presentation with multiple professional charts: bar charts for conversation counts, complexity, incident ratios, satisfaction ratings, and plan-level comparisons. The charts have clear titles, consistent color schemes, well-labeled axes, and integrated tables with numeric data. The visual layout is organized, with charts complementing narrative sections. The candidate's use of consistent formatting and professional appearance earns a clear advantage. Score: +3\n\nSub-dimension 2 (Chart appropriateness & accuracy): The baseline uses a simple grouped bar chart appropriate for comparing tag frequencies, but lacks sophistication. The candidate report employs multiple chart types suited to different analytical tasks: bar charts for comparing pre/post changes, grouped bars for plan-level analysis, and side-by-side comparisons. Charts accurately represent the data described in tables and text, with appropriate axis scaling and clear differentiation between upgrade/downgrade events. The visualizations directly support the analysis without misleading elements. The candidate demonstrates superior chart selection and encoding accuracy. Score: +2\n\nSub-dimension 3 (Text-visual synergy & insightfulness): The baseline report has minimal integration between text and visualization, with only a brief mention of the chart. The candidate report excels here, with explicit references to each chart (\"visualized in the plots below,\" \"as shown in Figure X,\" \"This visual confirms that...\"), detailed explanations connecting visual patterns to insights, and thoughtful annotations highlighting key takeaways. Each visualization is positioned to support specific findings, and the narrative effectively guides the reader through what to observe in each chart. This creates a cohesive, insight-driven experience. Score: +3\n\nTotal score: 8 (range -10 to +10). The candidate report shows markedly superior visualization quality, appropriate chart selection, and strong integration between visuals and narrative compared to the baseline's single, basic chart.",
